TASK-198 runtime harness: an IPv6-literal page (http://[::1]:<port>/) loaded
programmatically and through the command palette's real input path, with
its favicon, dev-mode row and faux address bar. Temporary code, never
committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task198-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # $SITE: index.html (no icon link), favicon.ico (16x16 red),
    # declared.html (<link rel="icon" href="/green.png">), green.png.
    python3 -m http.server 8898 --bind ::1 --directory "$SITE" > server.log 2>&1 &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify198 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8898 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher reads new lines of $OUT/verify.log every 0.2 s and runs
    # `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber> $OUT/<name>.png` for each
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line, and notes if the pid exits (a crash).
    # Wait for "done" (about 20 s), then kill that pid and the server.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task198-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify198

Steps: (1) TabStore.addTab(in:url:) with http://[::1]:8898/; (2) Cmd+T
(`newTab`), "[::1]:8898" typed key by key into the field editor
(`firstResponder.keyDown`, so interpretKeyEvents → insertText), Return
(keyCode 36 → insertNewline → PaletteSelection.returnAction →
didSubmitInput → AddressInputClassifier.directURL); (3) Cmd+L
(`focusAddressBar`), "http://[::1]:8898/declared.html" typed over the
selected prefill, Return. A Combine sink logs every favicon change of tab 1.

Results (2026-10-24, fresh profile, after the fix; both captures read):
- The app stayed alive through all three loads (before the fix the first
  load trapped in BrowserTab.load: URL(string: "http://::1/favicon.ico")!).
- Classifier: "[::1]:8898" -> http://[::1]:8898, "http://[::1]:8898/" as
  written; both are URLs, not searches.
- Step 1: url http://[::1]:8898/, faviconURL http://[::1]:8898/favicon.ico,
  16x16 icon; server log "GET /favicon.ico 200" from ::1 (served only on
  [::1]:8898, so brackets and port were right). Row: hazard border, host
  line "[::1]:8898"; faux address bar "[::1]" (read "::1" before the
  displayHost fix, seen in an earlier capture).
- Step 2: the palette listed the field text plus open-tab rows; Return
  opened a new tab at http://[::1]:8898/, same favicon (FaviconLoader cache,
  no second request).
- Step 3: in place, http://[::1]:8898/declared.html, faviconURL
  http://[::1]:8898/green.png (server: "GET /green.png 200"); same site key
  ([::1]:8898), so no second /favicon.ico guess. Declared icon reached the
  tab while WKSecurityOrigin.host is "[::1]" (bridge check now brackets the
  page host).
- On a fresh profile's first launch the favicon download's main-queue
  completion landed 0.1-5 s after the server answered (busy launch); one
  early run read nil at +2 s and had it by step 2. Not IPv6-specific.

